 "relevance_note": "A primary HLH cohort of 30 patients in which one identifiable patient carries a stated homozygous LPIN2 variant: \"In 1 patient, a homozygous LPIN2 mutation was detected, leading to a diagnosis of Majeed syndrome.\"",
 "method_note": "Hand-built from reading the paper (small output; a short script only assembled the JSON). Cohort of 30 primary HLH/IEI patients; only the single LPIN2 patient is in scope (no label, not a case report, so 'unnamed person 1'). The paper prints no LPIN2 variant description, so variant_original_string is 'not reported'; only zygosity 'homozygous' is stated for this person. No individual-level sex, age, consanguinity, treatment, HSCT or outcome is given for this patient; all such data are cohort aggregates and were not assigned. Phenotypic rows use only statements naming the whole cohort ('All patients had a fever lasting longer than 5 days', 'Ferritin was elevated in all patients', inclusion as primary HLH), with evidence_basis 'inferred from group statement'. Thrombocytopenia '30 (100%)' was not used because it is a count rather than a named-group statement. Fever lasting >5 days was not taken as 'recurrent fever'; CRP was elevated in 19/26 (count only), so the ESR/CRP checklist item is not reported; all checklist items are 'not reported'. Contradictions in the paper (cohort-level): consanguinity 21 (Abstract) vs 22 (Results, Table 2); causative gene identified in 19 (Results) vs 18 (Discussion); neurological involvement 5 (Results, Table 2) vs 4 (Discussion); PHA response tested in 7 (Results) vs 9 (Discussion, Table 2); CRP elevation 19 (63%) in text vs 19/26 (73.1%) in Table 2. Supplementary Table 1 is listed but its content is not in the file.",
